rvim is a Vim-compatible text editor in Rust. It has two licenses, chosen per
file. Each source file's first line is an SPDX identifier that says which one
applies. The arrangement follows Neovim's, which is Apache-2.0 for the project
with the parts contributed under the Vim license kept under that license. The
difference is that rvim marks each file, where Neovim's C sources carry no
per-file header. The Apache-2.0 grant covers all of rvim except the files
marked Vim below.

1. Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE). Applies to rvim's own code: every
   file whose first line is "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0".

2. Vim license (LICENSE-VIM). Applies to the files derived from Vim's C source
   or algorithms. Each of them has the first line
   "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Vim" and, on the second line, a note that it is
   derived in part from Vim and is a modified version. These files are:

   src/buffer.rs      mark adjustment for lowercase marks (Vim's mark_adjust)
   src/cmdline.rs     command-line history (Vim's histadd)
   src/editor.rs      editor state, undo and redo glue, Insert mode (Vim's u_sync, open_line, start_arrow)
   src/ex.rs          Ex commands; the :s loops port Vim's do_sub()
   src/jumplist.rs    jumplist and context mark (Vim's setpcmark, checkpcmark, cleanup_jumplist, movemark)
   src/motion.rs      word motions (fwd_word, bck_word, end_word), findmatchlimit(), utf_class table
   src/normal.rs      Normal and Visual commands (ports of Vim's normal.c nv_* functions)
   src/ops.rs         operators (Vim's ops.c and register.c)
   src/regex.rs       regular expressions (semantics follow Vim's backtracking engine)
   src/register.rs    registers (Vim's register.c)
   src/scroll.rs      scroll commands (Vim's scroll and halfpage logic; marked conservatively)
   src/search.rs      searchit(), do_search(), current_search() (ports of Vim's search.c)
   src/textobject.rs  text objects (ported from Vim's textobject.c)
   src/undo.rs        undo tree (Vim's u_undoredo model)

   The marking of buffer.rs, cmdline.rs, editor.rs, register.rs, regex.rs,
   scroll.rs and undo.rs is conservative. It is not an assertion that each
   line is a copy of Vim's code. The owner has not yet reviewed these files
   line by line against Vim's source.

Vim is by Bram Moolenaar and the Vim contributors (https://www.vim.org). The
Vim license text, with Vim's own notices, is in LICENSE-VIM. It is unchanged.

This is a modified version of Vim, not the official Vim. For bug reports
